  abstract = {Dietary components have been implicated in many biological processes, including development, organogenesis, and homeostasis. Dietary intake of specific natural products safely reduces the risk of developing a wide range of human diseases. However, the exact molecular mechanisms by which these natural agents function in human health have not been clearly defined. Recent findings have suggested that the dietary intake of natural products contributes to the prevention and treatment of diseases by regulating the RNAi pathway. In this review, we summarize recent findings regarding the potential of natural products for the treatment of several types of human diseases, which may lead to the development of innovative therapies. In addition, we discuss the potential of novel miRNA-based therapy for diseases using natural products and propose a new aspect of miRNA research involving natural products as miRNA regulators.},
